{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372111-ongoing-question","id":372111,"title":"ongoing question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-16T01:43:55-08:00","id":372111,"title":"ongoing question","content":"I have been asking this for a while and have not been given any response, so I am still wondering - why was there no UDE discussed in the KS for Wr20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T06:27:09-08:00","id":372254,"title":"","content":"Because no one wants this book to become one of their fetters? No, I don't know, but you should rather ask this question to the Deadguy himself in the topic 'Ask the Deadguy'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4701-dam","name":"Dam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T07:55:31-08:00","id":372503,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the fact that there was not Wraith ( revised edition) probably had an impact too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T09:04:42-08:00","id":372588,"title":"","content":"My acronym understanding is a bit lacking so what does UDE stand for here?<br /> <br /> UDE: Unified Development Environment<br /> UDE: Urban Design Element<br /> UDE: Unix Desktop Environment<br /> UDE: Uncorrectable Data Error<br /> UDE: Ultimate Dashboard Exploit<br /> UDE: Universal Debug Engine<br /> UDE: University of Denver<br /> UDE: Understanding the Digital Economy<br /> UDE: ultrasonicated dry egg<br /> UDE: Unreal Development Environment<br /> UDE: untoward drug effects<br /> UDE: urinary desmosine excretion<br /> UDE: Ubiquity Developer Edition<br /> UDE: unidad de empleo<br /> UDE: Urea-denatured antigen E<br /> UDE: University Department of Education<br /> UDE: User Defined Edge<br /> UDE: Universal Design in Education<br /> UDE: Upper Deck Entertaiment<br /> UDE: Universal Data Entry<br /> UDE: User Defined Events<br /> UDE: User Defined Entity<br /> UDE: Union Des Entreprises<br /> UDE: Uni\u00f3n Democr\u00e1tica Espa\u00f1ola<br /> UDE: University of Dakota Energy<br /> UDE: University of Delaware Entomology<br /> UDE: Unlimited Doreen Eubank<br /> UDE: Utah Department of Environment<br /> UDE: Utility Dog Excellent<br /> <br /> Or perhaps:<br /> UDE University of Duisburg-Essen (Rhine-Ruhr region; Germany) <br /> UDE Undesirable Effects (Goldratt: Theory of Constraints) <br /> UDE Universal Data Exchange <br /> UDE Unidad de Desarrollo Educativo (Spanish: department of education) <br /> UDE Utilisation Durable de l'Energie (French: Sustainable Use of Energy; Belgium) <br /> UDE Undetected Character Error <br /> UDE Underwater Detection Establishment (Great Britain) <br /> UDE Undetected Disk Error <br /> UDE Universidad de la Empresa (Spanish: University of The Company; Uruguay) <br /> UDE Upper Deck Entertainment (Carlsbad, CA)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T09:18:07-08:00","id":372591,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I think it means &quot;Ultra Deluxe Edition.&quot; Personally, I'm rather partial to &quot;Utility Dog Excellent,&quot; but that's just me...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T10:47:44-08:00","id":372731,"title":"","content":"Ah.. That explains it.<br /> <br /> Though I like both Utility Dog Excellence and <a href=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/7521803\" target=\"_blank\">Ultrasonicated Dry Egg</a>.<br /> <br /> Still nice to know what we are discussing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T03:27:15-08:00","id":373442,"title":"","content":"No, you are all barking up the wrong obelisk, its Unnameable Demonic Entity.<br /> This question has been put too many times (on KS, Facebook and various other portals) and has been ignored, leaving the sense that this was intentional as other questions posted at the same time received responses.<br /> Me, I would not mind one as a fetter, it would be better than many of the living people I know.<br /> And I can understand if there are reasons why there was no ultra deluxe, even though we havent been told what they are, my question is also really about why there was no discussion about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T07:36:11-08:00","id":373456,"title":"","content":"While I'm a fan of the extra special deluxe books, they have so far been a massive sink of time and energy for the design teams to actually make work. W20 basically didn't hit its 200 goal for them, but got close enough Rich sucked it up and did it; and then the HME had massive delays. M20 did make the 200 goal, but not by a huge margin and Rich still had to spend considerable time getting the lenticular card to work (and isn't even able to start the process of making sure it embeds into the cover properly).<br /> <br /> Given the sense that Wr20 and C20 are not going to demand as big of a crowd as the &quot;big three&quot; it seems sensible to not put out that much effort for something that had good odds of not happening. This seems to be holding fairly true. W20 and Wr20 had similar numbers of backers; W20 didn't actually hit 200 books for its HME. M20 had over 1,500 more backers and solidly made enough to get it. It would be nice to have seen ultra deluxes for at least the original five cWOD books, but it doesn't really seem like the numbers are there to justify the effort. Three data points isn't really enough, but it seems like the KS needs to hit ~2,500 backs to hit them solidly, and most cWOD KSs don't hit that many backers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T14:39:13-08:00","id":373800,"title":"","content":"It could also be they're afraid of the Wraith Curse and after the headaches of W20 don't want to go through again but somehow worse.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T03:20:22-08:00","id":377085,"title":"","content":"But none of that explains why they practically refused to discuss it with the community by ignoring backers inquiring about it...it kind of grates now hearing all the talk about 'open development' and 'listening to backers' when in this case they were not even prepared to say anything, and still have not...why no discusion, when questions were repeatedly put, across all platforms? Were they planning something as a surprise that did not transpire? Ok, why not say so now?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T04:38:47-08:00","id":377115,"title":"","content":"I fear you may be the only one, or one of the very few, requesting such a feature. Not many are actually interesting in an UDE, and probably the efforts don't worth it.<br /> That said, you could still ask the developpers to give you the contact of the company which made the UDE for W20, or simply search any company able to do so once Wr20 is available in pdf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4701-dam","name":"Dam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T07:55:37-08:00","id":377239,"title":"","content":"&quot;Open development&quot; is not an Oynx Path policy, it's something each development teams makes their own choices about. Some consider it worth doing, some don't, and there are reasonable cases on both sides. The more intensive the revisions really are, the less open development tends to be. The reasoning here is pretty obvious in that the fan community's random feedback isn't terribly useful because it tends to default to assuming everything is like the previous edition until a change is presented. The sheer amount of time needed to put extremely revised content up to community feedback with enough context for the community to give valuable feedback is often not worth it. Wr20 is probably in that category given the lack of a Revised edition leaving a lot of updating to bring it in line with the other 20th edition books.<br /> <br /> &quot;Listening to backers&quot; isn't the same as answer every question. That's sort of in the definition of the words involved. This is something you are kind of ignoring to say that nothing addresses your disappointment. The backers that want the UDEs are, generally, a constant but small percentage of the backers. The practical requirements of making the UDEs isn't something we, as the backers, have said is valuable enough to be worth doing every time. Most Onyx Path Kickstarters do not generate enough backers, to get enough UDE backers, to meet the minimum print run of 200. Not offering a UDE to avoid the W20 situation of being a few short of 200 and having to pick between no HME and disappointing a lot of backers or eating the financial cost of the last few books is listening to the backers.<br /> <br /> And frankly, UDEs aren't a development thing. They're a swag thing. There's nothing to discuss. Either it will happen for a book or it doesn't.<br /> <br /> As for not answering: there's a simple bit of PR logic there. The answer is basically &quot;no&quot; unless they say otherwise. If they wait for a project to hit X backers before Y date (aka what seems to be the sweet spot when UDEs work), they can announce they're going to do it and get a nice big bump on the Kickstarter. If they never hit that point, they can just go on without it.<br /> <br /> What answer are you looking for, really?<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Dam - making your own UDE is both extremely expensive and questionable in practicality. Getting a simple print shop to do a nice print up of a clearly copyrighted PDF can be a significant pain despite it often being perfectly legal (IIRC all of the Onyx Path books are legal to print you own copy of as part of OneBookShelf's licensing). Getting a vanity press to not only do a proper printing, but to do a modified one with a custom cover using copyrighted logos and trademarks is going to be to questionable for most to allow it. Designing your own custom leatherette cover and slapping either the Wr20 logo on it, or any Onyx Path/CCP trademark on it, is pretty much a fast track to getting a C&amp;D or sued; meaning any vanity press is going to keep the hell away from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T09:38:34-08:00","id":377282,"title":"","content":"I _did_ answer right at the beginning of the KS. I had no plans for one because I didn't see a need, unlike W20 and M20 where there were cover treatments I'd never tried creating for you all. Once I said that, previous KSs indicated that backers would respond to any additional questions as Heavy did here; basically providing you with sufficient answers. Then if a backer did hit on a concept that shone, like with M20, it might be something to include during the course of the KS. And as Heavy said, without that cool cover idea I have to seriously weigh whether disappointing backers, and the very tedious process of refunding them if we can't do it, is worth it. Sorry if my trying to cover all those bases was frustrating, we'll try and improve that next time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T10:18:02-08:00","id":377340,"title":"","content":"Wraith already got it's fancy cover edition........it was 1st Edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T14:47:13-08:00","id":377550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372111-ongoing-question?p=377340#post377340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraith already got it's fancy cover edition........it was 1st Edition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. I got to do my fancy glow in the dark design idea from the start with Wraith, so a heavily embossed full chain pattern for the deluxe sounds pretty Deluxe to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T12:37:51-08:00","id":378284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372111-ongoing-question?p=373456#post373456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W20 and Wr20 had similar numbers of backers</div> </div> </div> </div>To put this into some perspective, the <b>Werewolf</b> Kickstarter actually had fewer backers (150, give or take) than the <b>Wraith</b> project, but the <b>Wraith</b> pledges were maybe 80% of those for the <b>Werewolf</b> project. As stated, the pledges for <b>W20</b>'s Ultra Deluxe didn't meet its required mark, but it was close enough that Rich graciously (<i>maybe</i> selfishly 'coz he wanted to make it) allowed the thing to go through. Now, is it possible that the <b>Wraith</b> one could have raised more with an offered Ultra Super Version? Maybe, but...<br /> <br /> The <b>Mage</b> Kickstarter \u2013 totally hitting its threshold for the Ultra Deluxe \u2013 had around TWICE that backers of the <b>W20</b> AND made much more in pledges. The idea that Rich approved for the <b>M20</b> Ultra Deluxe combined elegance and a level of feasibility into something that could be offered for the price that would be truly special. As I recall (and please feel free to correct me if I'm wrong), the <b>M20</b> campaign had already blown expectations out of the water by the time discussion of the Ultra Deluxe came up, making it a shorter bet than it would have been for the <b>Wraith 20</b>, which STILL blew away expectations, needless to say.<br /> <br /> ...Of course, all of the above adds little to what has already been stated, but I felt it worth mention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T14:07:30-08:00","id":378374,"title":"","content":"Anything worth mentioning is worth mentioning often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T08:40:17-08:00","id":379059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372111-ongoing-question?p=377239#post377239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What answer are you looking for, really?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Really, the one that came after yours <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But thanks for taking the time to share your thoughts with me, I appreciate that. I dont expect every question to be answered, but given the fact that other deluxes had been given this treatment I thought it was a fair one to ask and one which collectors would want to know about. And the KS proved that assumption to be correct. So I was asking why there was no disucssion, and Rich has answered that for me: there was, but it was not very clearly communicated to the public, and the holiday season probably had a lot to do with that part too.<br /> And I dont think assuming that no answer is by default a flat no is all that much help when the creators are actually asking for ideas and dont have all the time they would like to respond. There might also be surprises in stretch goals planned, which was talked about in the comments as a possible reason for why nothing had been said. See we did not know, or at least, it seemed most of us did not know.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/372111-ongoing-question?p=377282#post377282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I _did_ answer right at the beginning of the KS. I had no plans for one because I didn't see a need, unlike W20 and M20 where there were cover treatments I'd never tried creating for you all. Once I said that, previous KSs indicated that backers would respond to any additional questions as Heavy did here; basically providing you with sufficient answers. Then if a backer did hit on a concept that shone, like with M20, it might be something to include during the course of the KS. And as Heavy said, without that cool cover idea I have to seriously weigh whether disappointing backers, and the very tedious process of refunding them if we can't do it, is worth it. Sorry if my trying to cover all those bases was frustrating, we'll try and improve that next time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I really appreciate that, this was not known to me, nor to many of the other backers I have spoken with. I had heard rumours that you had said something but nobody could actually point out the quote. Maybe if the crowd had been better informed they might ave wracked their brains and come up with something, but as it was not many seemed to know this was the case.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}